WEBVTT

00:10.208 --> 00:13.083
[♪ sinister music playing]

00:35.583 --> 00:36.583
[screams]

00:37.167 --> 00:39.875
[distorted vocalizing]

00:44.208 --> 00:45.208
[Smee] Wait.

00:46.083 --> 00:48.167
-[screams]
-[Siberian grunts]

01:06.875 --> 01:08.208
[gulls shrieking]

01:38.417 --> 01:41.250
[♪ dramatic music playing]

02:01.792 --> 02:03.625
[alien screeching]

02:27.167 --> 02:28.250
[Dame Sylvia sighs]

02:45.083 --> 02:48.458
It's just growing pains, that's all.

03:00.417 --> 03:02.125
[creature growling]

03:09.375 --> 03:11.000
[gunshot]

03:12.375 --> 03:14.167
-[alien screeches]
-[soldiers screaming]

03:14.250 --> 03:15.958
-[soldier] Clear.
-[Rashidi] Are you okay?

03:20.125 --> 03:23.000
It's not safe here, ma'am. Let's, uh…
Let's get you back to the facility.

03:40.208 --> 03:41.542
[Atom Eins] Comms are down.

03:43.917 --> 03:46.833
We think the Cyborg cut
the underwater trunk line.

03:48.417 --> 03:50.833
Yutani is jamming the satellites.

03:51.917 --> 03:53.125
We're cut off.

03:54.417 --> 03:58.375
Nonessential personnel…
have been evacuated.

04:00.292 --> 04:03.667
The hybrids are confined
in holding cell one…

04:04.458 --> 04:07.542
but it wasn't designed
for synthetic beings.

04:09.083 --> 04:10.792
I'm not sure how long it will hold

04:10.875 --> 04:12.583
if they decide to break out.

04:14.167 --> 04:17.458
We have zero containment
on the adult Xenomorph.

04:19.833 --> 04:22.667
Prodigy forces are sweeping the island,

04:23.250 --> 04:24.542
but they're running short of men.

04:27.000 --> 04:28.292
It keeps killing them.

04:29.542 --> 04:32.083
Containment on the other creatures
is good for now.

04:32.167 --> 04:34.000
But we're understaffed.

04:34.833 --> 04:38.625
-And negative variables are increasing.
-[goat bleats]

04:38.708 --> 04:41.458
I think you should consider evacuating.

04:44.375 --> 04:46.875
Sir? Sir?

04:46.958 --> 04:48.542
[Marcy, on recorder]
I'm going to the moon?

04:48.625 --> 04:51.250
[Boy Kavalier laughs on recorder]
No, silly.

04:51.333 --> 04:54.417
You're gonna be the first person
to transition from a human body…

04:55.333 --> 04:56.333
to a synthetic.

05:05.833 --> 05:07.250
[creature bleating]

05:12.958 --> 05:14.458
I wish I could hear your voice.

05:16.917 --> 05:18.417
The things you've seen.

05:20.292 --> 05:23.833
Yeah, that really would
be an interesting fucking conversation.

05:26.250 --> 05:27.833
[♪ dramatic music playing]

05:31.833 --> 05:32.917
[clicks tongue]

05:57.958 --> 05:58.958
[grunts]

06:03.958 --> 06:06.208
What did you do?

06:14.958 --> 06:16.542
[Curly] Okay, I know why they're in here.

06:16.625 --> 06:18.583
Don't know what you did,
something dumb probably.

06:18.667 --> 06:19.667
[Smee] Tsk.

06:19.750 --> 06:21.667
But I'm the favorite,
I shouldn't be in here.

06:22.458 --> 06:25.500
-Maybe it's because you snitched.
-Snitched?

06:26.333 --> 06:28.625
-I didn't snitch.
-[Smee] Snitched on who?

06:28.708 --> 06:32.167
They knew right where to find us
'cause you ran and told.

06:32.250 --> 06:35.125
-Did not.
-Wait, did-did you tell on us too?

06:35.208 --> 06:36.708
No, I don't even know what you did.

06:37.292 --> 06:39.375
[Nibs] You're the only one we told.

06:39.458 --> 06:40.875
[Curly] Okay, I didn't.

06:40.958 --> 06:42.875
Maybe if I did,
I wouldn't be in here with you.

06:44.125 --> 06:45.500
[Wendy] We found our graves.

06:47.417 --> 06:52.000
Rose, Marcy, Chris, Aarush…

06:54.500 --> 06:55.500
and Jane.

06:56.750 --> 06:58.458
-You.
-I'm not dead.

07:03.042 --> 07:06.292
She gave us each a flower
and up you go on the table.

07:06.375 --> 07:08.417
[Curly] No, they saved us,
and now we can't die.

07:09.208 --> 07:10.583
Isaac died.

07:13.875 --> 07:15.458
-[Slightly sniffles]
-He died.

07:20.333 --> 07:21.708
[Slightly] His name was Steven.

07:25.417 --> 07:27.250
His mom called him Steve-O.

07:28.167 --> 07:29.417
Okay, well, that's not gonna happen to us.

07:29.500 --> 07:31.042
It could. A fly ate his face!

07:33.292 --> 07:34.292
[Wendy sniffles]

07:35.667 --> 07:38.750
No, okay? I'm the favorite.
I'm not supposed to be here.

07:38.833 --> 07:42.375
No, in the book, Wendy Darling
is Peter Pan's favorite.

07:44.750 --> 07:46.292
And then she grew up.

07:47.750 --> 07:51.792
And that made Peter mad,
and so he kidnapped her daughter, Jane.

07:56.583 --> 07:59.625
We're all in this cell
because we can't be kids anymore.

08:01.125 --> 08:02.542
But they won't let us be adults.

08:04.333 --> 08:05.500
We're all ghosts.

08:11.792 --> 08:14.292
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

08:16.375 --> 08:18.000
What do ghosts do?

08:23.958 --> 08:25.333
They haunt houses.

08:30.917 --> 08:32.000
All this time,

08:33.167 --> 08:34.500
we've been afraid of them.

08:40.000 --> 08:41.958
But I think they should be afraid of us.

08:42.042 --> 08:44.042
[♪ ominous music playing]

09:12.000 --> 09:13.833
[Wendy screeching]

09:23.417 --> 09:26.167
[alien screeches]

09:29.500 --> 09:30.667
[computer beeping]

09:31.542 --> 09:32.792
[Boy Kavalier] Huh?

09:34.667 --> 09:36.083
Uh…

09:41.167 --> 09:42.708
-[computer beeping]
-No, no.

09:44.458 --> 09:45.958
No. [sighs]

09:46.042 --> 09:47.708
-Kirsh.
-Sir?

09:48.333 --> 09:50.708
The security feeds are down.
Are the creatures tucked in?

09:50.792 --> 09:53.500
We're on our own power supply down here.
All lights green.

09:53.583 --> 09:55.167
I'm acclimating the new Xenomorph.

09:55.667 --> 09:56.708
And the Cyborg?

09:57.292 --> 09:59.042
[Kirsh]
In a holding cell with the brother.

09:59.875 --> 10:04.708
It's risky. Yutani, she'll come for him.
As far as we know, ships are on the way.

10:04.792 --> 10:06.625
Oh, yeah. So you think
I should just give him back?

10:06.708 --> 10:09.625
He came here to kill us all
and steal our toys!

10:09.708 --> 10:10.708
[Kirsh] You're mad.

10:11.792 --> 10:14.167
Don't be mad. Be smart.

10:15.083 --> 10:16.542
Me?

10:17.042 --> 10:18.333
Brain the size of a planet.

10:18.917 --> 10:22.000
Why don't you grow some balls?
She wants to fuck with me?

10:22.083 --> 10:24.750
Yutani, huh? Let's fucking go!

10:24.833 --> 10:27.042
[radio static]

10:27.125 --> 10:31.417
Sir, a defining symptom
of ADHD as severe as yours

10:31.500 --> 10:34.208
is impulse control problems.

10:34.917 --> 10:36.625
And the choices you've made…

10:36.708 --> 10:39.167
[radio static interference]

10:39.417 --> 10:40.458
…the hybrids…

10:40.542 --> 10:42.250
-Kirsh?
-[static]

10:42.333 --> 10:44.333
-[Kirsh] Your medication…
-[static]

10:45.208 --> 10:47.708
Kirsh? Kirsh?

10:50.333 --> 10:53.333
Morons. They're all…
They're all morons. [scoffs]

11:00.750 --> 11:02.292
How do you feel about your eyes?

11:03.333 --> 11:04.750
Sir?

11:07.083 --> 11:08.333
Uh, find Atom.

11:09.667 --> 11:13.083
Tell him we need to reboot comms
and cameras, and to come find me.

11:17.875 --> 11:20.375
Just to be safe,
I think I'll feed you someone weak.

11:38.208 --> 11:40.125
-[Siberian] Clear.
-I'm fine, really.

11:40.208 --> 11:41.417
Keep the doors locked.

11:42.042 --> 11:43.333
Alert's a hard orange.

11:43.833 --> 11:45.958
We're prepping nonessential personnel
for exfil.

11:46.917 --> 11:48.458
I volunteer to ride the wing.

11:48.542 --> 11:49.542
Knock it off.

11:50.042 --> 11:52.750
We need to find other assets
and secure Mr. Kavalier.

11:53.625 --> 11:55.500
Stay here, ma'am. We'll be back soon.

12:04.375 --> 12:06.667
[breathing shakily]

12:15.917 --> 12:18.375
[inhales deeply, sighs]

12:19.792 --> 12:24.667
It's amazing here.
Everyone is so homely, and it's so cozy.

12:25.167 --> 12:28.875
I'm not really sure. I've got
mixed emotions 'cause I feel like…

12:29.583 --> 12:30.667
I'm not really sure.

12:30.750 --> 12:34.417
I feel like that I'd be able to do really
cool things,

12:34.500 --> 12:36.750
and, like, have super powers.

12:36.833 --> 12:38.375
I'd really like to be invisible

12:38.458 --> 12:40.208
cause then I could sneak up
behind people

12:40.292 --> 12:42.958
and go to really fun places
without anyone.

12:43.042 --> 12:45.583
-[Dame Sylvia panting]
-We'll be okay.

12:48.250 --> 12:49.250
Won't we?

12:51.750 --> 12:52.750
Won't we?

12:54.167 --> 12:55.167
Won't we?

12:55.875 --> 12:56.917
We'll be okay.

12:59.583 --> 13:00.667
Won't we?

13:03.125 --> 13:04.458
Won't we?

13:05.500 --> 13:06.542
Won't we?

13:08.542 --> 13:09.708
We'll be okay.

13:12.208 --> 13:13.208
Won't we?

13:15.792 --> 13:16.792
Won't we?

13:18.125 --> 13:19.125
Won't we?

13:19.208 --> 13:20.292
We'll be okay.

13:20.375 --> 13:22.292
[grunts, breathes shakily]

13:35.000 --> 13:36.167
-Hey.
-[gasps]

13:36.250 --> 13:39.250
-[groans]
-It's okay. Let me have a look.

13:39.333 --> 13:41.875
It's the best I'm gonna feel all day.
Let me enjoy it.

13:45.000 --> 13:46.333
[groaning]

13:48.042 --> 13:49.042
[Morrow sighs]

13:50.833 --> 13:51.875
You okay?

13:53.333 --> 13:54.500
I've had better days.

14:03.833 --> 14:05.750
Were you really on that ship
when it crashed?

14:07.000 --> 14:08.833
That's a yesterday conversation.

14:09.625 --> 14:10.792
I don't look back.

14:12.042 --> 14:13.042
You shot me.

14:15.417 --> 14:16.667
I saved your life.

14:19.750 --> 14:20.750
How's the lung?

14:22.000 --> 14:23.167
[intercom beeps]

14:27.333 --> 14:28.542
[Morrow] The boy told me.

14:30.333 --> 14:31.375
Aarush.

14:32.167 --> 14:33.833
Feels good, doesn't it?

14:35.000 --> 14:36.208
Being more than human.

14:37.667 --> 14:38.958
Hermit, there is a price.

14:39.750 --> 14:43.583
When the corporation gives you something,
there's always a price.

14:43.667 --> 14:44.917
Do you know what it is?

14:46.125 --> 14:49.042
-Everything.
-[Morrow laughs]

14:50.083 --> 14:52.042
"Everything" doesn't begin to cover it.

15:05.125 --> 15:06.917
-[radio static]
-Command, this is TR-1, come in.

15:07.000 --> 15:09.042
[indistinct radio chatter]

15:09.125 --> 15:10.125
-Command--
-[shushes]

15:10.208 --> 15:11.417
[clattering]

15:18.625 --> 15:20.208
[♪ ominous music playing]

15:21.583 --> 15:23.833
[Siberian] Comms are down.
What should we do?

15:24.333 --> 15:26.917
Protocol is to rally at the armory on one.

15:27.542 --> 15:29.083
With those things running around?

15:29.167 --> 15:31.167
Just fight the battle
that's in front of you.

15:31.250 --> 15:34.000
-Hey. I don't wanna die here.
-Hey. I got you.

15:34.083 --> 15:35.875
Be somebody's dinner?
I didn't sign up for that shit.

15:35.958 --> 15:38.625
Let's just get to the armory
and get the big guns.

15:39.417 --> 15:40.792
[elevator beeps]

15:49.583 --> 15:50.708
Did you call it?

15:51.292 --> 15:52.667
I guess God saved me the trouble.

16:04.917 --> 16:06.250
Come on.

16:07.167 --> 16:08.500
You're letting the cold air out.

16:26.417 --> 16:28.250
-[elevator stalls]
-[bell ringing]

16:33.750 --> 16:36.583
[intercom beeps]
Self-destruct sequence initiated.

16:37.250 --> 16:39.583
-This elevator will explode in 30…
-Open the door! Open the door!

16:40.708 --> 16:42.417
-…twenty-nine, twenty-eight…
-Open the door!

16:42.500 --> 16:45.792
-Come on! Come on!
-…twenty-seven, twenty-six.

16:46.625 --> 16:49.500
Twenty-five, twenty-four.

16:49.583 --> 16:50.792
-Boost me up.
-Twenty-three…

16:50.875 --> 16:52.458
-Hurry!
-Twenty-two…

16:53.083 --> 16:55.208
-Twenty-one.
-Hey. Stop fucking around.

16:55.292 --> 16:56.417
[chuckles] Twenty.

17:06.250 --> 17:07.792
-[alarm blaring]
-[Siberian] What the fuck?

17:23.042 --> 17:24.042
You mad at him?

17:24.875 --> 17:26.250
He shot Nibs.

17:30.000 --> 17:31.417
Yeah, 'cause she killed someone.

17:31.500 --> 17:33.750
-He chose them.
-Yeah, but…

17:35.167 --> 17:36.167
he's one of us.

17:51.833 --> 17:52.917
[Marcy] Dear Joe,

17:54.625 --> 17:55.667
I hope you're good.

17:57.500 --> 17:58.500
Are you good?

18:00.667 --> 18:01.875
We're okay, I guess.

18:03.333 --> 18:04.542
The nurses here are nice,

18:05.125 --> 18:06.375
except one.

18:06.458 --> 18:08.917
She uses the S-word… a lot.

18:10.375 --> 18:12.708
The mashed potatoes are pretty good
and the Jell-O.

18:13.417 --> 18:14.500
Cherry is my favorite.

18:16.083 --> 18:17.250
Dad's been home mostly.

18:18.167 --> 18:19.333
His cough is worse.

18:20.250 --> 18:21.292
And the leg.

18:22.208 --> 18:23.542
He says it's nothing,

18:23.625 --> 18:26.125
but it looks bad, and he can't visit much.

18:27.958 --> 18:31.167
Sorry to say only bad news.
I'm trying to stay happy,

18:31.250 --> 18:32.750
but I get so lonely here,

18:33.250 --> 18:34.500
and I get scared at night.

18:35.542 --> 18:38.792
The radiation treatments are awful,
and I get so sick after.

18:39.833 --> 18:41.167
I wish you could come home.

18:42.875 --> 18:44.167
Can't you just come home?

18:45.250 --> 18:46.833
[Hermit's father]
You gotta take care of her.

18:46.917 --> 18:47.917
Love, Marcy.

18:48.458 --> 18:53.292
[Hermit's father] You gotta take care
of him, don't you, Marcy? Yeah.

18:59.125 --> 19:00.333
[clicks open]

19:03.833 --> 19:04.958
Wait.

19:06.083 --> 19:10.333
Friend, you wouldn't have a cigar,
would you? A nice Cohiba?

19:10.958 --> 19:11.958
Shut up.

19:12.458 --> 19:16.417
Yeah, you're right, but I gotta pee
and this asshole won't unzip me.

19:16.500 --> 19:17.708
[guard grunts]

19:18.750 --> 19:19.917
[grunts]

19:20.000 --> 19:21.333
-[Joe] Oh, shit!
-[grunts]

19:21.417 --> 19:23.167
-Stop. You're gonna kill him.
-[grunts]

19:24.292 --> 19:25.583
Don't touch me!

19:28.292 --> 19:30.750
[breathes heavily]
I'm gonna save the ones I can.

19:32.750 --> 19:34.000
You better save the children

19:34.083 --> 19:36.167
'cause I'm gonna burn this place
to the ground.

19:43.000 --> 19:45.000
[♪ ominous music playing]

19:45.917 --> 19:47.333
[cocks gun]

20:12.667 --> 20:14.667
[electricity crackles]

20:53.250 --> 20:54.250
-[gunshot]
-[grunts]

20:56.667 --> 20:57.875
[Morrow grunts]

21:00.000 --> 21:01.208
[grunts]

21:01.292 --> 21:03.042
[both panting]

21:04.792 --> 21:06.458
[breathing heavily, grunting]

21:07.958 --> 21:09.417
[grunting]

21:19.875 --> 21:23.167
-[grunts]
-[breathes heavily]

21:27.833 --> 21:29.542
[Morrow grunts]

21:30.917 --> 21:33.083
[grunts, gurgles]

21:34.542 --> 21:35.625
[creature screeches]

21:37.125 --> 21:39.958
You know the story of John Henry
and his ten-pound hammers?

21:40.458 --> 21:42.083
[grunting]

21:42.167 --> 21:44.542
All night long, he drove that steel,

21:48.833 --> 21:49.833
fighting the machine.

21:49.917 --> 21:51.792
Who can dig deeper, faster?

21:54.333 --> 21:58.375
In the end, man will always win.
It's a question of will.

21:59.125 --> 22:03.417
[distorted] Didn't John Henry
die of exhaustion?

22:04.000 --> 22:05.583
Well, I'm just getting started.

22:06.250 --> 22:08.708
Yutani the younger's troops
are already on their way.

22:09.292 --> 22:11.958
And on her behalf,
I reclaim what is rightfully ours.

22:12.042 --> 22:13.500
[glass shattering]

22:16.125 --> 22:17.750
[creature chittering]

22:24.083 --> 22:25.750
[Morrow grunting]

22:32.500 --> 22:34.833
[Morrow breathes heavily]

22:36.500 --> 22:39.500
[♪ dramatic music playing]

22:46.125 --> 22:48.417
[Boy Kavalier] Oh, children!

22:52.500 --> 22:55.250
[chirping]

23:11.125 --> 23:12.917
Well, hell.

23:14.333 --> 23:16.667
Look at this sad debacle, huh?

23:17.667 --> 23:19.833
All my Lost Boys…

23:21.292 --> 23:22.417
locked in a cage.

23:26.083 --> 23:27.500
Who am I supposed to play with?

23:28.958 --> 23:30.125
[Smee] You wanna play?

23:32.125 --> 23:33.375
Well, let us out.

23:36.542 --> 23:38.417
Yeah, but will you play nice?

23:41.042 --> 23:42.292
Hmm.

23:42.375 --> 23:43.750
How about a story instead?

23:43.833 --> 23:44.833
[Curly] No.

23:45.875 --> 23:47.792
You're a liar.
You said I was your favorite.

23:47.875 --> 23:49.833
Oh, did I? Doesn't sound like me.

23:49.917 --> 23:51.208
Hmm.

23:51.292 --> 23:55.042
[stutters] Maybe… Maybe I did.
I ju… [sighs] Who can remember? [chuckles]

23:56.792 --> 23:59.000
[Wendy snaps fingers]

24:00.083 --> 24:01.125
What's the story?

24:04.833 --> 24:07.125
[♪ ominous music playing]

24:15.708 --> 24:17.167
Listen. [sighs]

24:18.583 --> 24:23.250
When I was little, my daddy was a drunk.

24:24.333 --> 24:25.417
Hmm.

24:27.333 --> 24:29.958
Yeah, the last in a long line
of mouth breathers,

24:30.042 --> 24:31.417
each meaner than the last.

24:33.000 --> 24:37.917
And to this troglodyte was born a miracle.

24:39.917 --> 24:43.708
A boy genius destined to rule the world.
[chuckles softly]

24:44.625 --> 24:46.792
Unless his jealous daddy killed him first.

24:48.208 --> 24:51.250
So the boy, me, built a machine.

24:51.333 --> 24:52.542
My first Synth. I was six.

24:52.625 --> 24:55.333
I made him, you know, a grown man.

24:56.750 --> 24:57.750
Distinguished.

24:58.875 --> 24:59.875
And, uh…

25:00.583 --> 25:04.583
Yeah, one day, my daddy…
came home from the factory.

25:07.625 --> 25:09.375
And there was my Synth…

25:11.083 --> 25:12.625
sitting on the sofa.

25:12.708 --> 25:13.875
[♪ sinister music playing]

25:15.500 --> 25:16.958
And that was the end of Daddy.

25:21.375 --> 25:23.417
Or should I say old Daddy
because that night we moved

25:23.500 --> 25:25.042
and the Synth became my new daddy.

25:26.667 --> 25:28.625
You see… [scoffs] …no one…

25:29.125 --> 25:32.417
no one's gonna give a six-year-old
his own empire, so…

25:33.792 --> 25:35.750
I just made myself a figurehead.

25:39.583 --> 25:43.500
-You killed your father?
-No. The point isn't who killed who.

25:43.583 --> 25:46.458
The point is I'm running
a multitrillion dollar business,

25:46.542 --> 25:50.125
and that's before people find out
they can be immortal for a low, low price.

25:50.208 --> 25:52.125
[Nibs] We don't belong to you.

25:53.750 --> 25:55.000
Of course…

25:55.875 --> 25:57.167
you do. Sweeties…

25:59.208 --> 26:00.542
you're floor models.

26:02.167 --> 26:06.000
These beautiful bodies can be yours
if you act now, but you're fucking it up.

26:06.083 --> 26:08.958
You're fucking it up!
And I… I can't have that.

26:10.250 --> 26:12.250
-[bodyguard] On the ground.
-[Nibs growling]

26:13.625 --> 26:15.000
Careful now. [chuckles]

26:15.083 --> 26:16.333
Now.

26:16.417 --> 26:18.667
-[growling]
-[gunshot]

26:20.208 --> 26:22.083
[bodyguard screaming]

26:26.042 --> 26:27.042
[chuckles]

26:28.875 --> 26:29.917
Run.

26:31.917 --> 26:33.917
-[♪ suspenseful music playing]
-[chuckles]

26:35.750 --> 26:36.917
[Smee growls]

26:37.917 --> 26:39.167
Hide-and-seek, remember?

26:40.208 --> 26:41.250
Nibs,

26:42.250 --> 26:43.333
you find Sylvia.

26:44.250 --> 26:45.542
I'll take care of Boy K.

26:46.250 --> 26:47.417
Smee, Slightly…

26:48.083 --> 26:49.458
you find Kirsh and the Cyborg.

26:50.500 --> 26:51.500
Curly.

26:52.000 --> 26:53.083
You get the soldiers.

26:53.917 --> 26:54.917
Jane.

26:56.500 --> 26:57.500
My name's Jane.

27:04.542 --> 27:05.917
Nobody touches my brother.

27:11.917 --> 27:15.958
Mr. Hermit. I've been looking for you.

27:18.417 --> 27:20.792
Mr. Kavalier asked me
to find you personally.

27:23.250 --> 27:25.167
He has a proposal he'd like to make.

27:28.833 --> 27:30.417
Your sister is with him.

27:34.417 --> 27:35.458
Please.

27:40.042 --> 27:41.375
This way.

27:41.875 --> 27:43.917
I think you'll like what he has to say.

27:56.083 --> 27:57.333
You think he's still there?

27:58.542 --> 27:59.542
Who?

28:00.792 --> 28:01.917
Arthur.

28:03.500 --> 28:04.667
We just left him.

28:06.042 --> 28:07.125
Don't think about it.

28:09.000 --> 28:10.458
We did a bad thing, Slightly.

28:13.458 --> 28:14.875
It's not our fault.

28:16.250 --> 28:17.333
They made us.

28:20.667 --> 28:21.708
It's not our fault.

28:33.583 --> 28:35.625
[soldier] Move, move, move!

28:39.417 --> 28:42.750
-[soldiers screaming]
-[gunshots]

28:45.167 --> 28:47.167
[raindrops pitter-patter]

29:07.042 --> 29:09.042
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

29:21.667 --> 29:23.083
[gasps]

29:28.583 --> 29:30.667
[Kirsh grunting]

29:35.917 --> 29:37.417
[breathes heavily]

29:43.958 --> 29:45.833
[distorted]
Where were you ten minutes ago?

29:46.833 --> 29:48.000
Why is he on the floor?

29:49.583 --> 29:51.333
-His back's broke.
-Hmm.

29:51.417 --> 29:53.042
Take this and tie him up.

29:53.583 --> 29:55.208
Quick, before he comes to.

30:10.292 --> 30:11.625
What are you doing?

30:13.458 --> 30:16.667
Your time is done. It's our time now.

30:26.417 --> 30:28.792
I just want you to know
I didn't hurt your mother.

30:43.833 --> 30:46.000
I don't want to spoil the surprise, but…

30:47.000 --> 30:48.542
I think you'll like Mr. Kavalier's offer--

30:48.625 --> 30:50.292
I'm not leaving without my sister.

30:51.375 --> 30:53.000
And we wouldn't dream of asking.

30:57.458 --> 30:59.417
We're not monsters.

31:00.458 --> 31:02.500
We realize your sister has rights.

31:03.042 --> 31:05.250
Let me guess, the lung's free now…

31:06.042 --> 31:07.708
but you're gonna take everything else.

31:08.958 --> 31:10.125
Go on in.

31:11.042 --> 31:12.417
I'll give you some privacy.

31:25.125 --> 31:26.125
Hello.

31:32.375 --> 31:33.583
Hello?

31:39.208 --> 31:40.667
[creature screeching]

31:49.583 --> 31:51.083
[bleating]

31:55.292 --> 31:58.250
[screech-bleating]

31:59.375 --> 32:00.875
[screeching]

32:00.958 --> 32:02.833
[squelching]

32:05.208 --> 32:07.208
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

32:31.875 --> 32:33.292
[grunting]

32:44.208 --> 32:45.250
[glass shatters]

32:45.750 --> 32:46.750
Help!

32:50.250 --> 32:51.583
[both breathing heavily]

32:54.083 --> 32:55.542
[♪ ominous music playing]

33:03.792 --> 33:04.792
[Wendy grunts]

33:08.417 --> 33:10.542
I told him it was a waste of technology.

33:12.292 --> 33:14.708
Who would make children immortal?

33:15.625 --> 33:18.375
An eternity of, "Are we there yet?"

33:19.667 --> 33:21.292
But he's a child at heart.

33:22.208 --> 33:24.250
Our founder. God bless him.

33:25.000 --> 33:26.667
Far be it from me to know better.

33:27.667 --> 33:30.583
But were my programming
to allow me to say…

33:32.333 --> 33:33.792
"I told you so."

33:36.000 --> 33:37.458
[♪ dramatic music playing]

33:40.833 --> 33:42.125
-No!
-[♪ music stops]

33:56.208 --> 33:57.708
I say what happens now.

34:01.042 --> 34:02.917
You don't get to hurt us anymore.

34:08.875 --> 34:11.083
Joe. Joe?

34:19.750 --> 34:21.042
What's wrong with him?

34:26.000 --> 34:30.958
He's mechanical, and he's on the network,
just like the doors, and the cameras.

34:34.125 --> 34:35.458
I can make him do what I want.

34:37.958 --> 34:41.042
-Huh. [chuckles]
-[chuckles]

34:42.667 --> 34:45.958
Marcy, I'm… I'm sorry about Nibs.

34:46.667 --> 34:47.667
I…

34:48.292 --> 34:49.750
I didn't have a choice.

34:49.833 --> 34:51.125
You're supposed to help people.

34:53.667 --> 34:54.792
I did.

34:55.500 --> 34:56.958
Nibs was hurting my friends.

34:57.042 --> 35:01.708
-Are you saying Nibs… isn't people?
-That's not what I said.

35:01.792 --> 35:04.292
-Maybe you should call me "it."
-Stop!

35:04.417 --> 35:07.583
I didn't make the world.
You sound like a child.

35:07.667 --> 35:10.167
It's better than being greedy
and lying to everyone.

35:10.250 --> 35:11.958
What would you like me to do?
The world is…

35:12.042 --> 35:15.000
It's complicated. Life is complicated.

35:15.083 --> 35:16.500
You wanna know why I like them?

35:19.042 --> 35:20.375
The aliens.

35:22.458 --> 35:23.792
They're honest.

35:28.458 --> 35:29.667
They're predators.

35:30.500 --> 35:32.125
We're food to them.

35:32.625 --> 35:34.500
No, you're food to them.

35:35.417 --> 35:36.417
I'm…

35:40.667 --> 35:42.250
I don't know what I am.

35:44.833 --> 35:46.125
I'm not a child.

35:47.417 --> 35:48.583
I'm not a grown-up.

35:49.583 --> 35:50.958
I'm not Marcy.

35:52.667 --> 35:53.917
I'm not Wendy.

35:56.042 --> 35:58.875
And I can't be
what everyone wants me to be.

36:01.583 --> 36:03.292
Okay. I'm sorry.

36:04.917 --> 36:07.042
I fucked up.
I didn't know what else to do.

36:08.125 --> 36:10.000
-It's comp--
-Don't say complicated.

36:12.167 --> 36:16.000
That is what powerless people say
to make doing nothing okay.

36:17.792 --> 36:19.000
And I'm not powerless.

36:25.208 --> 36:27.958
We have to go.
We're rounding up the grown-ups.

36:28.042 --> 36:29.042
Where's Boy?

36:31.042 --> 36:32.208
Hide-and-seek.

36:33.625 --> 36:35.708
I've got someone special looking for him.

37:00.083 --> 37:01.417
Whoo!

37:02.000 --> 37:03.375
Okay, this is the founder.

37:03.458 --> 37:05.958
I'm moving to the airship.
My, uh, body man is down.

37:06.042 --> 37:08.208
A million dollars to the first man
that finds me.

37:19.625 --> 37:22.167
[♪ ominous music playing]

37:25.667 --> 37:26.917
[alien chittering]

37:33.917 --> 37:37.083
-[banging]
-[growling]

37:47.708 --> 37:50.042
[growling]

38:10.083 --> 38:12.000
-[Wendy clicking]
-[screeches]

38:12.417 --> 38:13.833
Uh!

38:14.792 --> 38:16.958
-[gunshots]
-[soldiers screaming]

38:22.667 --> 38:26.083
Whoa! I think I pissed myself.

38:27.000 --> 38:28.000
[Boy Kavalier gasps]

38:31.375 --> 38:32.792
A little help, kid.

38:33.542 --> 38:34.750
Huh? [chuckles]

38:36.042 --> 38:37.042
[grunts]

38:37.125 --> 38:38.708
[door chimes]

38:44.458 --> 38:45.625
Stay frosty.

38:46.750 --> 38:48.125
This is a bad place.

38:49.792 --> 38:50.792
I'll take left.

39:08.042 --> 39:09.542
[Rashidi] Security services.

39:11.083 --> 39:13.583
-Anyone here?
-[♪ suspenseful music playing]

39:17.833 --> 39:18.833
[grunts]

39:18.917 --> 39:21.167
[coughing]

39:22.917 --> 39:25.333
[burbling]

39:35.500 --> 39:37.125
[burbling intensifies]

39:37.208 --> 39:40.750
[creature screeches]

39:44.333 --> 39:46.000
-[gunfire]
-[Siberian screaming]

39:53.417 --> 39:54.667
Fuck!

40:02.792 --> 40:04.125
[clatters]

40:28.042 --> 40:30.042
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

40:30.125 --> 40:33.125
[squelching]

40:49.917 --> 40:53.167
[soldier on radio] Yutani leader inbound.
Prepare for invasion and recovery.

41:23.625 --> 41:26.208
Wendy… darling.

41:26.792 --> 41:29.375
-Whatever I did, I'm sorry.
-No, you're not.

41:30.417 --> 41:32.667
You think you're a good person
who did good things.

41:33.917 --> 41:35.875
All you did is put six children
in the ground.

41:43.125 --> 41:44.458
I figured it out.

41:45.542 --> 41:46.667
Your game.

41:48.667 --> 41:50.125
You're not Peter Pan.

41:52.167 --> 41:54.542
He was a boy who never grew up, but you…

41:57.000 --> 41:58.500
You were never a boy.

42:02.042 --> 42:03.542
You've always been a man.

42:05.125 --> 42:08.333
A mean, angry little man…

42:16.083 --> 42:17.958
who decided to hate everybody.

42:20.167 --> 42:21.250
Just like your daddy.

42:26.625 --> 42:28.042
That's…

42:29.750 --> 42:31.500
[exhales heavily] You gonna let her, uh…

42:32.333 --> 42:34.250
You gonna let her talk to me like that?

42:39.625 --> 42:40.750
Huh?

42:49.708 --> 42:51.667
The plant monster
and the eye thing got away.

42:55.208 --> 42:58.083
But they can't hurt us.

43:11.583 --> 43:12.750
What do we do now?

43:32.125 --> 43:33.625
Now we rule.

43:33.708 --> 43:35.708
[♪ "Animal" playing]

43:38.458 --> 43:39.625
[chuckles]

43:42.667 --> 43:45.250
♪ One, two, three, four
Five against one ♪

43:45.333 --> 43:47.042
♪ Five, five, five against one ♪

43:47.125 --> 43:49.083
♪ Said one, two, three, four
Five against one ♪

43:49.167 --> 43:51.500
♪ Five, five, five, five
Five against one ♪

43:52.375 --> 43:58.667
♪ Torture from you to me, yeah ♪

44:01.417 --> 44:08.000
♪ Abducted from the street ♪

44:14.542 --> 44:16.750
♪ I'd rather be ♪

44:16.833 --> 44:18.917
♪ I'd rather be with ♪

44:19.000 --> 44:24.417
♪ I'd rather be with an animal ♪

44:32.958 --> 44:37.292
♪ Why would you wanna hurt me? ♪

44:42.000 --> 44:47.125
♪ So frightened of your pain ♪

44:55.167 --> 44:57.458
♪ I'd rather be ♪

44:57.542 --> 44:59.708
♪ I'd rather be with ♪

44:59.792 --> 45:04.375
♪ I'd rather be with an animal ♪

45:04.458 --> 45:06.542
♪ I'd rather be ♪

45:06.625 --> 45:08.708
♪ I'd rather be ♪

45:08.792 --> 45:14.667
♪ I'd rather be with an animal ♪

45:22.333 --> 45:24.625
♪ I'd rather be ♪

45:24.708 --> 45:26.875
♪ I'd rather be with ♪

45:26.958 --> 45:31.583
♪ I'd rather be with an animal ♪

45:35.875 --> 45:37.917
♪ Said one, two, three, four
Five against one ♪

45:38.000 --> 45:39.792
♪ Five, five… five, five… ♪

45:40.542 --> 45:41.542
[♪ "Animal" ends]
